Old content-free auto-memory notes no longer reach the system prompt. On this repo the memory block went from 20 lines to 2. Build, test (7122 passed, 0 failed), clippy and fmt all pass, and it's committed as 6788a1c5.

What I measured first: the store holds 20 old notes from before #1106:
• 9 are bare thread '…' panicked at file:L:C: headers. The predicate the writer already uses rejects these.
• 9 were cut off by the old 120-character limit before the line number even finished (…panicked at src/comma…). The writer's predicate treats these as real content, because they don't match its location pattern and the writer never sees cut-off text. Reusing that predicate alone, as the task said, would have left half the old notes in the prompt.
• 2 are Watch fix: … fixed on attempt N notes. They're kept because they aren't panic headers.

The change (+12 lines in src/memory.rs, now 1987 lines, under the 2000 cap): format_memories_for_prompt skips an auto note if the writer's predicate rejects it, or if it's the cut-off shape. Notes saved with /remember are never skipped. If every note is skipped, it returns None, the same as an empty store. Nothing is written when memories are read, so the old notes still drop out through #1106's eviction.

Tests (in src/memory_evict_tests.rs):
• Both header shapes are absent, while a real auto note and a /remember note are present (compared as full strings).
• A /remember note that looks like a header is kept.
• A store with only headers returns None.
• A store with nothing to skip renders exactly as before. That test was green before the change.
• Two checks where I broke the code and put it back: turning the skip off failed the two skip tests by name, and removing only the cut-off clause failed them with "truncated header leaked". Both passed again once restored.

Docs: one sentence added to docs/src/usage/commands.md.

Left out, as stated in the commit:
• /memories still lists the old notes.
• The two Watch fix notes are still injected.
• A /remember note that happens to start with the exact [bug] Test expectation in \ opening counts as an auto note. This limit already existed in is_auto_entry`.

There's no open issue for these, and the task said not to write "Fixes" or "Part of #1106", so they're only recorded in the commit message.
